      "value": "NoCUART0 is a UART wrapper that bridges a NoC-style event-driven interface to a legacy 16550 UART core, handling drive/free handshaking and data repacking.",
      "explanation": "The module connects NoC event inputs (i_drvFNoc, i_freeFNoc) and data payloads (i_dataFNoc_51) through a chain of FIFOs and delay elements to drive the uart_instance (m16550s), and repacks UART data (ReceiveData, r_dataHigh) into a 51-bit output payload (o_data2Noc_51). The free signals propagate back through cfifo0 to o_free2Noc, indicating completion.",
